<title>USA: Kansas City Power &amp; Light Co Q3 net down.</title>
<headline>Kansas City Power &amp; Light Co Q3 net down.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in Thousands)</p>
<p>			Third Qtr Third Qtr  Nine Months Nine Months</p>
<p>			  1996	1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Operating Revenues $270,202   $277,670   $703,031   $681,881</p>
<p> Net Income	     36,208     57,656     88,406     99,239</p>
<p> Preferred Dividends     947	  991	2,839	3,039</p>
<p>Earnings Available</p>
<p>  for Common	    35,261     56,665     85,567     96,200</p>
<p>Average Number of</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding  61,902     61,902     61,902     61,902</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share     0.57	 0.91	 1.38	 1.55</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1996 earnings reduced by $0.26, and nine-month 1996 earnings reduced by $0.31, due to terminating the merger with UtiliCorp United Inc and continuing to defend against Western Resources Inc's hostile offer.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
